          "filter_linear": false,
          "scale_type": "source",
          "scale": 1
        },
        {
          "tree": "shaders_slang",
          "path": "misc/shaders/image-adjustment.slang",
          "sha256": "e608b1dd71d660d2ce8a77ee3e3a62ad5047d50a75adc8db7b4a1b7c1be83e2d",
          "filter_linear": false,
          "scale_type": "source",
          "scale": 1
        },
        {
          "tree": "shaders_slang",
          "path": "handheld/shaders/lcd-cgwg/lcd-grid-v2.slang",
          "sha256": "dc77b29530e5b771f12a5a2dd68c390805139bc25d84a30dead021fd38e581c5",
          "filter_linear": false,
          "scale_type": "viewport",
          "scale": 1
        }
      ],
      "requires": [
        "shaders_slang"
      ],
      "params": {
        "ia_black_level": 0,
        "ia_bright_boost": 0,
        "ia_luminance": 1.0,
        "ia_saturation": 1.3,
        "ia_target_gamma": 2.2,
        "lighten_screen": 0.5,
        "mode": 1,
        "response_time": 0.222,
        "gain": 1.45,
        "gamma": 2.2,
        "blacklevel": 0,
        "ambient": 0,
        "RSUBPIX_R": 0.96,
        "RSUBPIX_G": 0.45,
        "RSUBPIX_B": 0.45,
        "GSUBPIX_R": 0.45,
        "GSUBPIX_G": 0.96,
        "GSUBPIX_B": 0.45,
        "BSUBPIX_R": 0.45,
        "BSUBPIX_G": 0.45,
        "BSUBPIX_B": 0.88,
        "BGR": 0
      },
      "doc": {
        "why": "GBC response and color, a saturation lift, then the cgwg subpixel grid so the panel reads as a GBC LCD",
        "passes": "Colour passes stay at the native 160x144, unfiltered, and only the grid renders at the viewport: lcd-grid-v2 takes its LCD cell from its source size, so a viewport-sized source turns one cell into one screen pixel (no grid, flat lifted blacks, 1-px subpixel streaks). This is the upstream nds/3ds-lcd-grid-v2 structure.",
        "params": "Tuned on settled frames, with the core's own correction off (config/systems/gbc/shaders.json), so GBC colours pass this matrix once. lighten_screen 0.5 is Gambatte's default central frontlight (gamma 1.7), the brightness its correction used to add. Image-adjustment only lifts saturation: target gamma 2.2 equals its monitor gamma, so no per-channel gamma lift washes colours out (0.85 did, and saturation 3.0 then pushed HSV saturation past 1: 224,64,64 and 224,96,96 drew alike and orange drew red), and black level 0 keeps every base of its pow() at or above 0. Saturation 1.3 keeps every colour of the clip and bars cards under HSV saturation 1 after this matrix (the bars card's blue, the most saturated, at 0.90). Each lcd-grid-v2 channel lights its own third of a cell, so white needs light from the neighbours or clipped peaks: the subpixels leak 0.45 and gain 1.45 bring white to about 228 (224 at 4K) with about half of the red and green subpixel peaks at 255 and the row gaps and colour stripes still drawn. Red and green subpixels at 0.96 and blue at 0.88 keep the white slightly warm. blacklevel and ambient 0 keep black black."
      },
      "output": {
        "sha256": "f26a6a9be3918c3503fe0ab4a8ec7f2ff5de3a08e0b7fb3d3ee4516a513bf9de"
      }
    },
