      "doc": {
        "why": "GBA response, NSO color matrix, a saturation lift, then the cgwg subpixel grid so the panel reads as an AGB-001 LCD",
        "passes": "Colour passes stay at the native 240x160, unfiltered, and only the grid renders at the viewport: lcd-grid-v2 takes its LCD cell from its source size, so a viewport-sized source turns one cell into one screen pixel (no grid, flat lifted blacks, 1-px subpixel streaks). This is the upstream nds/3ds-lcd-grid-v2 structure.",
        "params": "The same grid as gbc/screen.slangp, tuned on settled frames, with mGBA's own correction pinned off (config/systems/gba/shaders.json). Image-adjustment only lifts saturation: target gamma 2.2 equals its monitor gamma, so no per-channel gamma lift washes colours out (1.2 did, and saturation 2.6 then pushed HSV saturation past 1 so 224,64,64 and 224,96,96 drew alike), and black level 0 keeps every base of its pow() at or above 0. Saturation 1.3 keeps every colour of the clip and bars cards under HSV saturation 1 after the NSO matrix (the bars card's blue, the most saturated, at 0.84). Subpixels leaking 0.45 with gain 1.38 give a white of about 226 with the row gaps and stripes still drawn; red and green subpixels 0.96 and blue 0.88 keep it slightly warm. blacklevel and ambient 0 take the lift off black (54 before)."
      },
      "output": {
