        "BRIGHTEN_LCD": 4.0
      },
      "doc": {
        "why": "3DS top screen: the crisp lcd1x grid at its brightest, the parallax-barrier panel reads sharper than the touch panel"
      },
      "output": {
        "sha256": "89136a8350725a81271ee4e457e938f2ca41bb865066dcd1ccb9a22fabd27766"
      }
    },
    "assets/shaders/n3ds/bottom.slangp": {
      "type": "slang_pipeline",
      "passes": [
        {
          "tree": "shaders_slang",
          "path": "misc/shaders/image-adjustment.slang",
          "sha256": "e608b1dd71d660d2ce8a77ee3e3a62ad5047d50a75adc8db7b4a1b7c1be83e2d",
          "filter_linear": false,
          "scale_type": "source",
          "scale": 1
        },
        {
          "tree": "shaders_slang",
          "path": "pixel-art-scaling/shaders/sharp-bilinear-simple.slang",
          "sha256": "d97d47b9f7b399d5bdb9c6d67d11393b80e3e2f4fbec7db4e364f0ccbb5907ae",
          "filter_linear": true,
          "scale_type": "viewport",
          "scale": 1
        }
      ],
      "requires": [
        "shaders_slang"
      ],
      "params": {
        "ia_luminance": 0.75
      },
      "doc": {
        "why": "3DS touch screen: the panel's light without a drawn pixel grid. The shell's bottom opening holds 320x240 at a fractional scale on every display (0.95x on the Deck, 1.4x at 1080p, 2.8x at 4K), where lcd1x's one-sine-per-game-pixel grid beats against the screen's pixels: top.slangp drew 18-px vertical and horizontal bands there (column profile 146..238 on a white card). Below one screen pixel per game pixel no grid can be resolved anyway.",
        "passes": "Image-adjustment runs at the native 320x240 and sharp-bilinear-simple resamples it to the screen: it samples each game pixel at its texel centre and filters only a band 1/max(floor(scale), 1) texel wide where two pixels meet. At a whole multiple, which the computed dual layouts use (1x to 5x), that is pixel exact; at the shell's 0.95x and 1.42x the band is the whole texel, plain bilinear, so no one-pixel line drops out (nearest sampling dropped 4 of 80 columns and 2 of 30 rows at 0.95x); at 2.84x it is half a texel, so a line card has half as many in-between pixels. Bilinear at viewport scale blurred every pixel of the computed layouts: a one-pixel line drew 4 px wide at 2x, peak 143 of 191.",
        "params": "ia_luminance 0.75 is the mean of top.slangp's grid ((4/5) x (16/17)), so both screens keep the same brightness"
      },
      "output": {
        "sha256": "9916159242361b6f0b1767bf1710c860210f3a3384379a9a8d9f89dfc783721a"
      }
    },
    "assets/shaders/nds/top.slangp": {
      "type": "slang_wrapper",
      "reference": {
        "tree": "shaders_slang",
        "path": "handheld/lcd1x_nds.slangp",
        "sha256": "e665adcb83e51ca2b1e54a618cd33a54c45cb55ded21b00f5b92bb51ded22e9f"
      },
      "requires": [
        "shaders_slang"
      ],
      "params": {
        "BRIGHTEN_LCD": 12.0
      },
      "doc": {
        "why": "DS screens: the NDS-tuned lcd1x grid",
        "params": "BRIGHTEN_LCD 12 keeps the column grid at +-7.7% instead of upstream's +-20%. The shell places both screens at the fractional fit scale (2.2x on the Deck), where a grid near two pixels a cell beats against the panel's pixel grid into 11-px vertical bands; the shallow grid keeps that beat below sight."
      },
      "output": {
        "sha256": "9cc7a4c7e491b270fb7710833d5139cbe3ce305d43e98e3a2234e12bf3ef0471"
      }
    }
